cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Dynamics Engine Conformance
message: >-
  If you use these results or references, please cite them using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parsons
    given-names: Noah
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7224-6040'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Noah-Parsons/dynamics-conformance'
url: 'https://noah-parsons.github.io/dynamics-conformance/'
abstract: >-
  A continuously running conformance service for multibody dynamics
  engines. Each new release of SymPy, MechanicsDSL, Drake and Project
  Chrono is installed automatically and scored against closed-form,
  library-independent references on pendulum chains, near-singular and
  extreme-mass-ratio systems, a cart-pole and a closed-loop slider-crank.
  Each answer is classified by whether a wrong result was reported as
  success.
keywords:
  - multibody dynamics
  - conformance testing
  - silent failure
  - differential testing
license: MIT
